  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/A6AE82">Remark <span data-tag="A6AE82">5.3.5.2</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a small $\infty $-category and $\kappa $ a regular cardinal. Then the Yoneda embedding $j: \calC \rightarrow \calP (\calC )$ factors through $\Ind _{\kappa }(\calC )$. This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/B64EA9" data-tag="B64EA9">5.1.5.2</a>, since $j(C)$ classifies the right fibration $\calC _{/C} \rightarrow \calC $. The $\infty $-category $\calC _{/C}$ has a final object and is therefore $\kappa $-filtered (Proposition <a href="/tag/3AD8B4" data-tag="3AD8B4">5.3.1.15</a>). </p>
